Query: What does the TPMS warning light on the dashboard mean?
Retrieved 5 chunks:
  [text] page 71 (similarity: 0.7037)
  [text] page 71 (similarity: 0.7037)
  [text] page 70 (similarity: 0.7001)
  [text] page 70 (similarity: 0.7001)
  [text] page 114 (similarity: 0.6949)
Rate limit hit — waiting 20 seconds and retrying...

Answer:
The TPMS warning light can mean several things:

1.  It comes on and blinks for 4 seconds if Tyre Pressure is LOW/HIGH, Tyre temperature is HIGH, or there is Tyre air pressure leakage. After 4 seconds, the symbol will continuously be on until the warning is present.
2.  It comes on and blinks for 20 seconds if the TPMS system has a fault or if a TPMS sensor is faulty/missing. After 20 seconds, the symbol will continuously be on until the fault is present, and you should take your vehicle to a TATA authorized service center. (nexon-2025-owners-manual.pdf, Page: 114, text)

Additionally, a “—” near all the tyre and tyre symbol will blink if the TPMS system has a fault/missing, and “TPMS ERROR” test warning comes ON for 4 seconds when the TPMS system has a fault. (nexon-2025-owners-manual.pdf, Page: 71, text) Finally, "HI" near to the respective tyre and tyre symbol will blink if the tyre temperature is High. (nexon-2025-owners-manual.pdf, Page: 70, text)

